                <pb facs="0522" n="422" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg422"/>

                <head>No. 290.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gibbs to Mr. Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lima, Peru</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-05-07"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 7, 1884</date>.
                        (Received May 29.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 95.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The French minister, on 30th ultimo, passed
                    a note to Minister of Foreign Affairs that he had received a telegram
                    authorizing him to recognize the Iglesias Government immediately. It is also
                    reported that the Argentine Republic has recognized this Government. I suppose
                    that all the governments of any importance in Europe and the American continent
                    have now recognized this Government.</p>
                <p>Nothing of importance in political matters to communicate at present.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>RICHARD GIBBS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
